{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "11", "m": "10", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "10", "M": "23", "S": "34"}}, "news": [{"title": "Bombay HC quashes stamp duty demands on Goregaon property transactions", "para": "The Bombay High Court has quashed stamp duty demands on property transactions in Goregaon that involved multiple agreements. Authorities initially treated the 2012 conveyances as new transactions instead of finalizing earlier agreements from 1985. The Court emphasized the importance of analyzing the entire chain of documents to understand the transactions. It ruled that the final conveyances only completed previous arrangements rather than initiating new sales.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/bombay-hc-quashes-stamp-duty-demands-on-goregaon-property-transactions/134865670?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-1291820/134865670.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "No RR rate hike, higher target, yet Maharashtra stamp duty collections near 50% of annual goal", "para": "In a remarkable display of economic activity, Pune's registration and stamps department is nearing half its annual revenue goal before Dasara, boasting figures of Rs33,387 crore as of October 8. This surge stems from a bustling real estate market, where more than 26 lakh documents were processed from April to September.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/no-rr-rate-hike-higher-target-yet-maharashtra-stamp-duty-collections-near-50-of-annual-goal/134865647?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-52916/134865647.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "New Town Kolkata development body flags 38 buildings for illegal commercial use", "para": "The New Town Kolkata Development Authority has flagged unauthorized commercial endeavors in 38 residential buildings. Inspections revealed that several owners neglected to secure permissions for commercial use, which should not exceed 40% of the buildings' total area. Additionally, numerous units were operating without necessary fire licenses, posing significant safety risks. Authorities stress the importance of obtaining prior approval for any commercial activities.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/commercial/new-town-kolkata-development-body-flags-38-buildings-for-illegal-commercial-use/134865632?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-250180/134865632.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "commercial"}]}